title: Drill — clear, record, recurse
chapter: 21
type: drill
skills: macro-recursive
par: 40
minutes: 5
reps: 6
vscode: six cursors, type, End, paste
open: status-labels.ts

@brief
Six status names need to become entries whose value is the name
itself:

    PENDING,    →    PENDING: 'PENDING',

Then `};`. Empty the register, record with a guard first and `@a`
last, play once. Six times, until `qaq` is automatic.

@keys
| `qaq` | empty register `a` |
| `^f,` | the guard: no comma on `};` |
| `@a` | last key of the recording, and then the run |

@hints
`^f,` then `s: '` `Esc`, `^yiw`, `$p`, `a',` `Esc`, `j`, `@a`, `q`.
The yank comes after the `s`, because `s` would overwrite it.
--
Play it with a single `@a`. If you are pressing it more than once, the
`@a` did not make it into the recording.

@solution
    j  qaq   qa ^f, s: ' <Esc> ^yiw $p a', <Esc> j @a q   @a   :wq<Enter>

Thirty-four keystrokes. The drill is the ritual: `qaq`, `qa`, guard, edit,
step, `@a`, `q`, `@a`. Skip the first `qaq` once and you will not skip
it again.

@start status-labels.ts
export const statusLabels = {
  PENDING,
  CONFIRMED,
  PAID,
  SHIPPED,
  CANCELLED,
  REFUNDED,
};

@expected status-labels.ts
export const statusLabels = {
  PENDING: 'PENDING',
  CONFIRMED: 'CONFIRMED',
  PAID: 'PAID',
  SHIPPED: 'SHIPPED',
  CANCELLED: 'CANCELLED',
  REFUNDED: 'REFUNDED',
};
